    "repo": "swesmith/benoitc__gunicorn.bacbf8aa",
    "problem_statement": "Config.set() method raises AttributeError for valid settings\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen trying to set configuration values using the `Config.set()` method, it raises an `AttributeError` claiming that the configuration setting doesn't exist, even for valid settings that are clearly defined in the configuration.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom gunicorn import config\n\nc = config.Config()\nc.set('reload_engine', 'poll')  # This should work but raises AttributeError\n```\n\nExpected behavior: The configuration value should be set successfully.\n\nActual behavior: Raises `AttributeError: No configuration setting for: reload_engine`\n\nThis affects all configuration settings and makes it impossible to programmatically set configuration values through the `Config.set()` method."
  },
